    "created_at": "2015-10-20T00:28:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-10-20T00:28:15Z",
    "body": "Disclaimer: I don't have a lot of background on this section of the spec.\n\nIt looks like the intent is to preserve a couple things at once:\n- Don't change the property more often than it is changed by the author\n- Have the property always be up to date\n\nThus, the only time `ctx.currentTransform` will change will be when the author sets it. And, whenever the transformation matrix changes, the current `currentTransform` matrix will be updated, including if it's an author-provided one.\n\nI can see why this might be problematic for implementations. But it also seems well-motivated and reasonably JavaScript-idiomatic. So, the answer to \"is this correct?\" would be yes, and \"why\" would be because it gives the above two properties.\n\nIf you're really unhappy with this, as a first implementer you can help us make it different. Maybe one solution would be to change it to a getCurrentTransform() method returning a DOMMatrixReadOnly, which would very explicitly be a snapshot.\n\n/cc @bzbarsky ... this has flavors of our usual live vs. snapshot, method vs. getter, mutable vs. immutable issue.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
